// ZGS - helper: Gram-Schmidt process on the columns of [H].
// In : [H] (m x n)
// Out: [I] = orthogonal vectors v1..vK (not normalised), [G] = orthonormal vectors,
//      K = number of vectors kept (columns that depend on earlier ones are dropped).
//      If K=0 both are the m x 1 zero vector.
// v_j = u_j - sum (u_j.v_i)/(v_i.v_i) v_i
// Uses: M N J L I X, ʟZD ʟZU ʟZV ʟZW
dim([H])→ʟZD
ʟZD(1)→M
ʟZD(2)→N
0*[H]→[I]
0*[H]→[G]
0→K
For(J,1,N)
Matr►list([H],J,ʟZV)
ʟZV→ʟZW
For(L,1,K)
Matr►list([I],L,ʟZU)
ʟZW-(sum(ʟZW*ʟZU)/sum(ʟZU²))*ʟZU→ʟZW
End
√(sum(ʟZW²))→X
If X>1ᴇ⁻9*max(1,√(sum(ʟZV²))):Then
K+1→K
For(I,1,M)
If abs(ʟZW(I))<1ᴇ⁻12*X
0→ʟZW(I)
ʟZW(I)→[I](I,K)
ʟZW(I)/X→[G](I,K)
End
End
End
{M,max(1,K)}→dim([I])
{M,max(1,K)}→dim([G])
